# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14), from the product owner's replay; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: Mail and Notes are a group, saved as view 2, as in the guide. Looking at it, someone opens a terminal, which floats
# over the group. They frame Safari and come back with the shortcut for view 2: the terminal is there, in front, and
# has the focus it had. (F57; before, only a single framed window kept its new windows.)
# Reference: T34 T52.
# The ring is an option (collab/QUESTIONS.md, Q29). Here it says where the keyboard is, and that the line is round that very window.
set focusRing true
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
zoom 102
out
save-view 2
open Term 500x400
expect floating 104
expect ring 104
zoom 101
expect hidden 104
view 2
expect visible 104
expect ring 104
# Inside the group only a part of what it opened over is showing.
zoom 102
expect hidden 104
out
expect visible 104
# Notes closes, and Mail alone is what is left of the group. The terminal stays with it.
close 103
flush
zoom 101
expect hidden 104
zoom 102
expect visible 104
